mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The Graduation Thesis is an important practice-oriented and research-based course in the nursing program, aiming to cultivate students’ ability to comprehensively apply fundamental nursing theories, professional knowledge, and research methods to solve practical nursing problems. Under the guidance of supervisors, students independently select research topics in areas such as clinical nursing practice, nursing management, or nursing education, and complete the entire research process, including literature review, research design, data collection and analysis, and thesis writing. Through this course, students are expected to master the basic concepts and methods of nursing research, enhance their clinical thinking skills, research competence, and innovative awareness, and lay a solid foundation for future clinical practice and further academic study.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
